-- CVTable: a record's vtable. cvtable: the slots and the one index the object's vtable pointer addresses, for a vtable this unit emits that has one address point and no thunks. cvtable-full: every other vtable: whether this unit emits it (false: its key function is defined in another unit, or nothing here refers to it), its address points, slots, virtual base offset offsets, VTT, construction vtables; with no slots at all: a polymorphic class Clang laid out no vtable for in this unit (nothing here constructs it or calls a virtual function of it)
data CVTable =
    cvt-none
  | cvtable (address-point : Word) (entries : List CVTEntry)
  | cvtable-full (emitted : Bool) (address-points : List CVAddrPoint) (entries : List CVTEntry) (vbase-offsets : List CVBaseOffsetOffset) (vtt : List CVTTEntry) (construction : List CCtorVTable)
